{"step_index":160,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:20:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T10:20:51Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T10:20:52Z\nShowing lines 1-100 of 414\n1: # PR30–44 independent deployment review\n2: \n3: Task: pr-sweep-20261023. Reviewer: /root/review_deployment. Snapshot: 2026-10-23T21:09:27.253Z.\n4: \n5: All **244 unresolved threads** were classified against their exact PR heads, cumulative tip `d46bd4b1483b845e9d2df1afc52c5dd9dab60582`, and recovery `86f03d2dede738e2d780ab789dd5800b58678479`. Full saved review bodies were also considered. All mandatory preload files and network policy were read. No builds, tests, formatting, Clippy, fixtures, live changes, GitHub mutations, or repository edits were performed during review.\n6: \n7: **Only #44 is an independent ready source delta.** Its security finding is a false positive; parent subsequently reports it merged into #43 at `8d1665a`. Other PR heads are not ready as submitted. Retired transport layers should be superseded, not repaired into active network policy.\n8: \n9: ## Implementation update — isolated source only\n10: \n11: Three commits on `codex/pr-sweep-deployment-20261023` in `/home/jeremy/.codex/worktrees/5ce9/odbus-verified` are ready for independent primary-agent review:\n12: \n13: - `6ff02e2`: all supplied PR39 validator findings plus PR40 signed-zero hashing. Preserve the existing object-key-order correction.\n14: - `f811665`: same-handle operation receipts, guest cron receipt consumption, quoted responder argv/current MQTT endpoint, Qdrant readiness portability, and last-good notebook summary.\n15: - `d2243a5`: bearer headers over stdin rather than curl argv in three helpers.\n16: \n17: **Superseded recommendation:** parent verified the jsonschema patch carries a required preserve_order equality correction and explicitly rejected dropping it. Earlier archive/drop wording below is historical and must not be followed. Keep the patch and tra