network.md explicitly retires GRE; the current WARP TLS door is10.0.0.2:8090. Smallest action: Keep the later dependency removals. Never restore GRE firewall admission as the fix.\n66: - **fixed by later stack layer** — `PRRT_kwDOUgxzzc6tptQZ`, `PRRT_kwDOUgxzzc6tqk8-`. [Exact head source](https://github.com/repr0bated/odbus-verified/blob/24b39021eb756707432a8f2d490c34c0ef9b9314/deploy/config/network.conf#L34). Later ovs-vswitchd/run uses the configured empty INTERNAL_PORTS, while ovsbr0-uplink/svc-addr/tun5 are listed retired at the tip. Recovery delegates OVS ownership to its base owner. Smallest action: Retain retirement and recovery network ownership; do not recreate absent service ports.\n67: - **fixed by later stack layer** — `PRRT_kwDOUgxzzc6tptQd`. [Exact head source](https://github.com/repr0bated/odbus-verified/blob/24b39021eb756707432a8f2d490c34c0ef9b9314/deploy/config/network.conf#L35). PR32 moves the bridge's Qdrant environment off the removed10.200.0.2 endpoint. Recovery bridge run:212–224 uses COGNITIVE_QDRANT_URL on127.0.0.1:6334, matching the owner correction. Smallest action: Use the later loopback configuration and current COGNITIVE_* names.\n68: - **needs decision** — `PRRT_kwDOUgxzzc6tptQi`. [Exact head source](https://github.com/repr0bated/odbus-verified/blob/24b39021eb756707432a8f2d490c34c0ef9b9314/deploy/config/agents/conf/threetched-fs@.service#L24). The guest unit intentionally runs as root (User=root:17). fuse_fs.rs:202,231–232 restricts calls to daemon/call-owner UID. The review assumes an unprivileged chatbot user, but no such supported caller is established; the current container-root identity boundary must be preserved. Smallest action: Do not add an arbitrary --call-owner-uid. Establish the intended guest caller UID first, then delegate only that UID if needed.\n69: - **fixed by later stack layer** — `PRRT_kwDOUgxzzc6tptQn`. [Exact head source](https://github.com/repr0bated/odbus-verified/blob/24b39021eb756707432a8f2d490c34c0ef9b9314/de