{"step_index":164,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:21:02Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T10:21:02Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T10:21:02Z\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 jeremy jeremy 4802 Oct 26 08:48 /srv/git/odbus-verified/deploy.sh\r\n#!/bin/sh\r\n# deploy.sh — the one command for deploying a prepared release.\r\n#\r\n#   sudo ./deploy.sh [--system]\r\n#\r\n# Run it after the release build and seal:\r\n#   CXXFLAGS=\"-include cstdint\" cargo build --workspace --release\r\n#   sudo target/release/opblob seal-shm && sudo target/release/opblob persist\r\n# OP_RELEASE_DIR selects one prepared optimized artifact directory for both\r\n# release-controller verification and golden preparation (default target/release).\r\n#\r\n# What it does:\r\n# 1. Native provision-slots reconciles any interrupted transaction and prepares\r\n#    the owned golden/slot layout. Recovery-only work stops this invocation.\r\n# 2. Prepares /opt/op-dbus/golden from target/release and the sealed catalog\r\n#    (internal helper deploy/lib/golden/build-golden.sh; it never builds or seals).\r\n# 3. Native deploy sends/receives the immutable generation into the inactive\r\n#    slot, rotates read-only overlays at the inventory's owned host targets,\r\n#    and restores affected consumers' wanted states. Only active + previous remain.\r\n# With --system, also apply the explicit base-file manifest transactionally and\r\n# request a graceful runit reboot only after durable activation success.\r\n#\r\n# Undo the last release:\r\n#   sudo /usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch rollback\r\nset -eu\r\nPATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin\r\nLC_ALL=C\r\nexport PATH LC_ALL\r\n\r\nREPO=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$(readlink -f \"$0\")\")\" && pwd)\r\nOP_RELEASE_DIR=$(realpath -e -- \"${OP_RELEASE_DIR:-\"$REPO/target/release\"}\")\r\nexport OP_RELEASE_DIR\r\nRELEASE_BASE=/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release\r\nRELEASE_LAUNCH=$RELEASE_BASE/op-release-launch\r\nRELEASE_BIN=$RELEASE_BASE/op-release\r\nRELEASE_BOOT=/etc/init.d/op-release-activate\r\n\r\n[ \"$(id -u)\" = 0 ] || { echo 'deploy.sh: run as root (sudo ./deploy.sh [--system])' >&2; exit 1; }\r\ncase \"$#:${1-}\" in\r\n    0:) ;;\r\n    1:--system) ;;\r\n    *) echo 'usage: deploy.sh [--system]' >&2; exit 2 ;;\r\nesac\r\n# Check the execution path before invoking any installed kit code. The launcher\r\n# independently checks the complete approved manifest and kernel/BTF pair.\r\nfor directory in / /usr /usr/local /usr/local/libexec \"$RELEASE_BASE\" /etc /etc/init.d; do\r\n    directory_mode=0$(stat -c %a \"$directory\")\r\n    [ -d \"$directory\" ] && [ ! -L \"$directory\" ] &&\r\n        [ \"$(stat -c %u:%g \"$directory\")\" = 0:0 ] &&\r\n        [ \"$((directory_mode & 07022))\" -eq 0 ] ||\r\n        { echo \"deploy.sh: insecure release-kit directory: $directory\" >&2; exit 1; }\r\ndone\r\nfor artifact in \"$RELEASE_LAUNCH\" \"$RELEASE_BIN\" \"$RELEASE_BOOT\"; do\r\n    [ -f \"$artifact\" ] && [ ! -L \"$artifact\" ] &&\r\n        [ \"$(stat -c %u:%g:%a:%h \"$artifact\")\" = 0:0:755:1 ] ||\r\n        { echo \"deploy.sh: install the approved root-owned release kit: $artifact\" >&2; exit 1; }\r\ndone\r\n# Authenticate the current kit before executing its launcher. In system mode\r\n# these approved bytes may differ from the incoming manifest-pinned kit.\r\nRELEASE_MANIFEST=$RELEASE_BASE/manifest.sha256\r\n[ \"$(stat -c %a \"$RELEASE_BASE\")\" = 755 ] &&\r\n    [ -f \"$RELEASE_MANIFEST\" ] && [ ! -L \"$RELEASE_MANIFEST\" ] &&\r\n    [ \"$(stat -c %u:%g:%a:%h \"$RELEASE_MANIFEST\")\" = 0:0:600:1 ] &&\r\n    [ \"$(stat -c %s \"$RELEASE_MANIFEST\")\" -le 1024 ] ||\r\n    { echo 'deploy.sh: insecure installed release-kit manifest' >&2; exit 1; }\r\nfor entry in \"$RELEASE_BASE\"/* \"$RELEASE_BASE\"/.[!.]* \"$RELEASE_BASE\"/..?*; do\r\n    [ -e \"$entry\" ] || [ -L \"$entry\" ] || continue\r\n    case \"${entry##*/}\" in\r\n        op-release|op-release-launch|manifest.sha256) ;;\r\n        *) echo \"deploy.sh: unexpected release-kit entry: $entry\" >&2; exit 1 ;;\r\n    esac\r\ndone\r\nawk '\r\n    BEGIN {\r\n        allowed[\"/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release\"] = 1\r\n        allowed[\"/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch\"] = 1\r\n        allowed[\"/etc/init.d/op-release-activate